course: dictionary
lesson: 15466
title: Stooping: one word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «Stooping» is a good example. «She was stooping down to tie her shoelace.» Here stooping means bending the top part of your body forwards and down.
explain: «The old man walked slowly, stooping over his stick.» This stooping means standing or walking with your back and shoulders bent forwards, often because of age or habit. The words old and slowly are the clues.
explain: «He would never stoop to cheating in a game.» Here stooping means doing something mean or dishonest, which is below your usual standards. Try the simple meaning in the sentence: «He would never bend down to cheating» does not make sense, so this must be the other meaning.
fact: Stooping means bending the top part of your body forwards and down.
fact: «Stooping» can also describe an older person who walks with a bent back.
fact: «Stooping to» means doing something mean, unfair or dishonest, such as «stooping to cheating».
fact: «Stooping low» means behaving in a mean or dishonest way.
fact: When you lift something heavy, bend your knees, not your back, so you do not hurt yourself.
exercise: «She was stooping down to tie her shoelace.» What does stooping mean here? | Running away quickly | *Bending the top of her body forwards and down | Standing very tall and straight | Jumping up and down
exercise: «He would never stoop to cheating in a game.» What does stoop to mean here? | Bend down to pick up a ball | *Do something mean and dishonest, below his usual standards | Laugh very loudly at the game | Walk with a stick
exercise: «The old woman walked slowly, stooping as she carried her shopping.» What does stooping mean? | Walking very fast | *Walking with her back and shoulders bent forwards | Singing a happy song | Sitting down on a bench
test: «The tall man had to go through the low door, stooping his head.» What does stooping mean here? | Running through the door quickly | *Bending his head and body forwards so he could fit | Standing on tiptoe to see over the top | Shouting loudly to his friends
test: «Lily would not stoop to telling lies, even to win.» What does stoop to mean here? | Be very tired after a long day | Bend down to the ground to find her coat | *Do something mean or dishonest
exam: In «He was stooping low to win by cheating», what does stooping low mean? | Hiding under the table | Bending very far down to the floor | Going to sleep early | *Behaving in a mean, dishonest way
